<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Coelba posts Q1 net vs loss.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Coelba posts Q1 net vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state electrical utility Coelba, owned by Bahia state, released the following first-quarter 1997 results, according to the Sao Paulo bolsa.</p>
<p>		  Q1 1997	     Q1 1996</p>
<p> Net profit    4.392 million	  loss 227.5 million</p>
<p> Net Revs    166.6 million		   159.4 million</p>
<p> Oper Profit   8.1 million		     4.5 million</p>
<p> Net Worth   907.2 million		   872.9 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in Brazilian reais, not adjusted for inflation.</p>
<p>Coebla, formally known as Companhia de Eletricidade do Estado da Bahia, is slated to be privatized on July 31.</p>
<p>Bid specifications for the auction are set to be released Friday.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
